COMMENT
  Bank Customer Churn - data cleaning and calculated fields in ACL Analytics
  Input : bank_churn_customers.csv imported as table Bank_Churn_Raw
          (Data > Data Definition Wizard; CustomerID as character,
           JoinDate and ChurnDate as dates YYYY-MM-DD, numeric fields as numbers)
  Output: Bank_Churn_Clean (12,480 records), exported to Diligent One Results
END

SET SAFETY OFF

COMMENT 1. Find duplicate customers
OPEN Bank_Churn_Raw
DUPLICATES ON CustomerID PRESORT TO "Dup_Customers" OPEN

COMMENT 2. Keep one copy of each customer
OPEN Bank_Churn_Raw
SORT ON CustomerID TO "Bank_Churn_Sorted" OPEN
EXTRACT RECORD IF CustomerID <> RECOFFSET(CustomerID, -1) TO "Bank_Churn_Dedup" OPEN

COMMENT 3-5. Count the invalid records
COUNT IF Age < 18 OR Age > 100
COUNT IF CreditScore = 0
COUNT IF Churned = 1 AND ChurnDate < JoinDate

COMMENT 6. Build the clean table
EXTRACT RECORD IF Age >= 18 AND Age <= 100 AND CreditScore > 0 AND NOT (Churned = 1 AND ChurnDate < JoinDate) TO "Bank_Churn_Clean" OPEN

COMMENT 7. Calculated fields used in the dashboard
DEFINE FIELD AgeGroup COMPUTED

"18-30" IF Age <= 30
"31-40" IF Age <= 40
"41-50" IF Age <= 50
"51-60" IF Age <= 60
"61-70" IF Age <= 70
"71+"

DEFINE FIELD CreditScoreGroup COMPUTED

"300-499" IF CreditScore < 500
"500-599" IF CreditScore < 600
"600-699" IF CreditScore < 700
"700-799" IF CreditScore < 800
"800-850"

DEFINE FIELD BalanceGroup COMPUTED

"1. Zero" IF Balance_JOD = 0
"2. Up to 5K" IF Balance_JOD <= 5000
"3. 5K-20K" IF Balance_JOD <= 20000
"4. 20K-50K" IF Balance_JOD <= 50000
"5. 50K+"

COMMENT 8. Export to Diligent One Results (replace the table ID and data center)
COMMENT EXPORT FIELDS ALL ACLGRC TO "<table_id>@<data_center>" OVERWRITE

SET SAFETY ON
